== what each holds ==
  integer  3
  real     0.1
  fraction 1|10
  float    0.1
  0.1 + 0.2 == 0.3   -> true
  0.1f + 0.2f == 0.3f -> false
== what converts on its own ==
  integer -> real     7
  integer -> fraction 7|1
  real -> fraction    1|10 and 1|4
  0.5 + 1|3           5|6
  1|3 + 0.25          7|12
  1|3 + 1|3 + 1|3     1|1
== what you have to ask for ==
  (1|3).ToReal()      0.3333333333333333333333333333
  and back to one?    false
  (1|4).ToReal()      0.25
  (0.1f).ToFraction() 3602879701896397|36028797018963968
  (0.5f).ToFraction() 1|2
== where a float differs ==
  1.0f / 0.0f         Infinity
  is it Infinity?     true
  -1.0f / 0.0f        -Infinity
  0.0f / 0.0f         NotANumber
  is it itself?       false
  largest integer     9223372036854775807
  largest real        79228162514264337593543950335
  largest float       1.7976931348623157E+308
